A||N||3||WhiteFieroBlur||Fastback clear tailights and cleaning||||5||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||11-13-2001||02:44 PM||||I am about to take off my GT tail lights I was wondering if anyone can tell me removal and instillation. and good cleaning procedures.<P>Also while they are off I want to stip off the colored parts and make em clear. Do I need to buy the new colored bulbs or can still use the stock ones? (I am thinking they are white bulbs, just not sure)<P>I really would love to get some like minngreen but I am not that talented  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Also does anyone have fast back pics of thier clear lights?||||reg||5
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||11-13-2001||03:06 PM||||Talented?  Well thank you!  <P>Removal and cleaning is simple.  First of all, remove the long screws located under the 6 black caps (above the lights/behind trunk opening/even with lock mechanism).  Then carefully pull the light back toward you.  All the lights can be removed by pinching the clip and twisting (the small 194's just twist out).  Once the assembly is removed, there are about 6 clips per assembly holding the pieces together.  You may need a fair amount of pressure to separate the assembly (black stuff is really sticky).  I didn't remove the black sealant, but left it on there to re-use (with the addition of some silicone sealant).  Inside there are 2 inserts: a red one for the "Pontiac" and a multi-color part for the brakes/signals.  Wash all components with warm soapy water (suggested: liquid dish soap).  Dry carefully (it scratches easily).  I also repainted some of my chrome reflector lenses because they were appearing burnt and/or worn (used "Crome Bumper Paint").  If you're going to leave out the multi-colored insert- you'll need colored bulbs. You'll need 1156 Bulbs for the Amber Turn signals, 1157 Red bulbs for the Brake/Tail lights, and the backups can remain white 1156 (or go to a "hyperwhite" like I did).  I'd also suggest a fresh set of 194's behind the pontiac.  Then reassemble the whole thing and stick it back together.<P>This is my original thread about the clear taillights and includes pics of the inital disassembly and associated parts.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010073.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010073.html</A> <P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TL_001.jpg">    <P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TL_002.jpg">    <P>Any more questions?  Be glad to help!  (BTW: you can always go back and add the diffuser lens later...)<P>[Shameless Plug]<BR>And for anyone who hasn't seen my finished pieces... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011212.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011212.html</A>  [/Shameless Plug]<P>------------------<BR>                 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif">    <p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 11-13-2001).]||||reg||1
